# Code Style Standards

## TypeScript for All New Files

Always use TypeScript. Never create plain `.js` files.

```typescript
// BAD
export function getUser(id) { ... }

// GOOD
export function getUser(id: number): Promise<IUser> { ... }
```

## Angular: Functional / Standalone Components

Prefer standalone components with `inject()` over class-based injection via constructor where possible.

```typescript
// BAD — old class-based injection style
@Component({ selector: 'app-foo', templateUrl: './foo.component.html' })
export class FooComponent {
  constructor(private userService: UserService) {}
}

// GOOD — standalone, inject()
@Component({
  selector: 'app-foo',
  standalone: true,
  templateUrl: './foo.component.html',
})
export class FooComponent {
  private userService = inject(UserService);
}
```

## Database Columns: snake_case

All database column names must use `snake_case`.

```typescript
// BAD
firstName: string;
createdAt: Date;

// GOOD
first_name: string;
created_at: Date;
```

When mapping DB results to TypeScript interfaces, convert to camelCase in the service/repository layer — keep the DB schema snake_case.
